{"seal": 20260829125737, "busker": "0.31.0", "type": "text/plain", "path": ["notes"]}

The sequence begins with the player standing on Harkness Island (44.8334, -75.31602) facing North.
A location to the West is a metal bridge across the weir, off the island. The high gate is securely locked.
To the East is a patch of ground covered with leaves and other litter.
At this location inspection of objects reveals evidence of a camp fire and the back story to a party.

On going North we meet a character sheltering under a tree. He is wearing a long cloak.
Conversation with the character reveals that he is waiting for workers to open the gate but that this might take hours.
At one point the locals had a spare key but it has been lost.

The sun regularly appears and when it does the stranger takes off the cloak. When clouds return he puts it on again.
Here is the opportunity to take the cloak. He seems not to mind.

On wearing the cloak at the campfire, the leaf litter brushes away to reveal a key.
This can be used to open the gate and escape the island.
There are two endings. If the player still wears the cloak the stranger appears and attacks. The player awakes with no
cloak and no key.

If the player drops the cloak at any location, there is no attack. This is the winning ending.

The game provides an inventory of all the random items collected at the camp fire. Points are allocated according to the
letters in their names.

